<title>USA: Kaman says picked for helicopter contract.</title>
<headline>Kaman says picked for helicopter contract.</headline>
<dateline>BLOOMFIELD, Conn. 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kaman Aerospace International Corp said Friday it has been selected as the preferred tenderer in a bid to supply a new generation of maritime helicopters for the Royal Australian Navy.</p>
<p>The company said contract negotiations are expected to begin shortly. The value of the contract has yet to be determined, it said.</p>
<p>Kaman said it has proposed supplying the SH-2G &quot;Super Seasprite.&quot; The contract calls for 11 multi-mission helicopters to go aboard Navy frigates.</p>
<p>The company said the helicopters are scheduled for introduction into service early next century.</p>
